  "interpretation": [
    "Yao setup medians were 3547.911 ms before, 3378.901 ms for the candidate, and 3354.236 ms after.",
    "The candidate was 169.010 ms faster than the first control and 24.665 ms slower than the second. Ranges overlap substantially.",
    "Every measured wallet reused already-started Router, A, B, and Signing Worker objects in all three arms.",
    "A performed preparation and execution in one object request. B preparation began after the initial A dispatch; fewer A entries did not remove all preparation dependencies.",
    "Signing Worker delivery medians were 572, 553, and 529 ms. Its first object-work medians were 123, 99, and 129 ms wall time.",
    "The outer Signing Worker package-handler CPU medians were 5, 2, and 3 ms. One first-control invocation used 77 ms CPU.",
    "The trace does not identify a serialization change that would remove the larger delivery delay.",
    "Router finish-dispatch medians were 49, 54, and 52 ms. Larger benefits from moving coordinator placement remain unmeasured; no regional coordinator resources or configuration were added.",
    "The two-second Yao setup target remains unmet."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Provider CPU and wall times describe whole invocations, not individual cryptographic operations.",
    "Application clocks freeze during CPU work; application spans are not transport timers.",
    "Small sequential samples do not establish a latency percentile or placement success rate.",
    "D1 counts cover bound-root loads only; total Gateway D1 and backend Console calls are unavailable.",
    "No diagnostic location fetches were added. Physical colocation is not proved.",
    "Per-operation CPU profiles and internal payload-byte counts are unavailable."
  ],
